From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XY55bqg6iAw8ttP <132220364+XY55bqg6iAw8ttP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Admit the J714c (apple,j714c) in developer builds:
 experimental, one machine

The 14-inch MacBook Pro with M5 Max (Mac17,7, J714c, j714cap, board 0x0a,
T6050) as a developer-only board, for one machine.

Apple's 27.2 restore image (26B123) carries the J714c: its j714cap
Customer identities (ApBoardID 0x0A, ApChipID 0x6050, iBoot.j714c
mBoot-20457.41.3). The release 10 kernel package ships t6050-j714c.dtb,
and the 27.2 G17C GPU build is upstream (aurora-silicon/linux, drm/asahi
hw/t6050.rs).

- Engine: j714cap device (27.2, expert off), j714cap on the 26B123 row
  beside j714sap, and the board 0x0a gate. BOARD_MACHO j714cap takes the
  J714s image's own Stage 1 members (stage1-j714s.{bin,macho}), as the
  J716s admission does: Stage 1 is chip-level and only chainloads the ESP
  Stage 2, whose device trees include t6050-j714c.dtb. The image is bound
  to the board by its installer_data (allowed_device_classes [j714cap]), so
  a J714s image is refused on a J714c and back.
- Camera setfiles and light-sensor calibration: the J714s collectors also
  run on the J714c (same IMX958 front camera and ALS).
- Centauri: the N1 FTAB is ticketed for j714cap/0x0a as for j714sap/0x08
  (apple/centauri/j714c-ftab.bin, the name the J714c device tree asks for).
- supported-models.json: apple,j714c as a developer board; MacModelNames:
  J714c; test_make_unsigned_catalog: the developer board set.
- Tests: the J714c board row, its Mach-O Stage 1 install, the refusals
  (J714s image on a J714c and back, wrong firmware, mixed metadata,
  missing members), the 26B123 row for j714cap, the Centauri ticket for
  j714cap and its board refusals, the J714c taking the J714s collectors.
- Engine v0.9.2-omarchy.20261125.c30af2262b3f (engine_pin.py name), rebuilt with
  rebuild-python-overlay.py from the authenticated engine.28 base:
  17915092 bytes, sha256 3666c451024e40dd15102e667013bdd127a9c887f1cb8297e37b03156f6afd6e, two identical rebuilds, prepare-engine.py
  reproduces it.

Checked: ./test/all (engine overlay 457 tests, 27 skips; scripts 306).
Signed-off-by: XY55bqg6iAw8ttP <132220364+XY55bqg6iAw8ttP@users.noreply.github.com>
